    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d689">

                <pb facs="0996" n="1504" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg1504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/10–2048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the United States
                        Delegation at Paris</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-21T19:00:00-05:00">October 21, 1948—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Gadel 266. Re Delga 421, Oct 20 we feel that we must abide by our commitments
                    under the Charter and by our statements last May and July advocating SC action
                    if necessary under Chapter VII to prevent further hostilities in Palestine in
                    defiance of SC in its efforts to preserve peace. We would much prefer however
                    not to play role of protagonist or have to speak first. This telegram has been
                    approved by the President.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d689-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d689-f1" n="1" xml:id="d689-f1-content">
                <p>Marginal notation: “Cleared by President 12:40 PM, Oct. 21”. The text of this
                    telegram was sent to London as No. 4058 the following day (501.BB
                    Palestine/10–2248).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
